{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788202185,"nonce":"xe5mO308YxEFV3Lp7BJz4XA0uWg=","message":"VERIFICATION (backlog verification pass, git-bug 2f2796e, run fbb2c59)\n\nCORRECTED — the citations in this issue are the most accurate in the backlog\n(every line number I checked resolved exactly), but there are FOUR corrections\nthat change work: one acceptance bullet is unsatisfiable, one recon instruction\nwould corrupt a correct citation, one piece of the work is already shipped under\na different name, and half the storage surface is already scoped by 3.2 and the\nissue does not say so.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 1 — \"REFUSED WITH THE GAME'S OWN REASON\" IS UNSATISFIABLE. THERE IS\nNO SUCH REASON FOR AN UNRESEARCHED PRODUCTION RECIPE.\n=====================================================================\n\nAcceptance bullet 2: \"A bill for a recipe whose research is not done is REFUSED\nwith the game's own reason, not queued.\"\n\nThe production-bill gate is `Verse/RecipeDef.AvailableNow` (a `bool`) and\n`Verse/RecipeDef.AvailableOnNow(Thing, BodyPartRecord)` (a `bool`). Neither\nproduces a string. The `AcceptanceReport`-returning variant —\n`Verse/RecipeWorker.AvailableReport(Thing, BodyPartRecord)` — exists but is used\nonly on the SURGERY path (`RimWorld/HealthCardUtility` calls it);\n`RimWorld/ITab_Bills` never does. Vanilla's behaviour for an unresearched\nproduction recipe is to OMIT THE ROW ENTIRELY from the options list. It authors no\nstring at all.\n\nThe only game-authored strings in this neighbourhood are\n`\"ClipboardBillNotAvailableHere\"` (the paste path), `\"RecipeRequiresMechanitor\"`,\nand `RecipeDef.MinSkillString`. So as written a worker cannot satisfy the bullet\nwithout inventing a reason, which contradicts \"the game's own\" and is exactly the\nthing `Blockers.cs`'s header refuses to do.\n\nReword it. Suggestion: *\"refused, naming the blocking `ResearchProjectDef.LabelCap`,\nwith the refusal explicitly marked as mod-authored because vanilla omits the row\nrather than explaining it.\"*\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 2 — THE RECON'S NAMESPACE CORRECTION AIMS AT THE WRONG TARGET AND\nWOULD BREAK A CITATION THAT IS RIGHT\n=====================================================================\n\nThe recon comment says: \"the body's `Verse/Bill.cs` citations are wrong\". The\nFILE LOCATIONS are confirmed — `Bill.cs`, `BillStack.cs` and `BillUtility.cs` are\nunder `RimWorld/`. But **the body as it now stands contains no `Verse/Bill.cs`\ncitation at all.** It writes `RimWorld/BillUtility.cs` and `RimWorld/BillStack.cs`\ncorrectly and cites `Bill.cs:29/156/165...` with no namespace. The body's ONLY\n`Verse/` citations are `Verse/RecipeDef.cs:241` and `AvailableOnNow (:398)` — and\n`RecipeDef.cs` IS under `Verse/`. A worker applying \"the body's `Verse/` citations\nare wrong\" as a rule will corrupt the one that is correct.\n\nWhere the `Verse/BillStack.cs` error actually lives is SHIPPED CODE:\n`Source/AutoRimmer/MedicalBillVerbs.cs`'s class header says \"`Verse/BillStack.cs\nAddBill` is four lines and checks NOTHING\" and \"from Verse/BillStack.cs\nDoListing\". That is the file the correction should have named. (Its\n`Verse/Pawn.cs` citation for `BillStack =\u003e health.surgeryBills` is correct.)\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 3 — `RecipeAvailableNow` IS ALREADY WRITTEN. THE WORK IS A MOVE, NOT\nA FRESH IMPLEMENTATION.\n=====================================================================\n\nThe recon says: \"`WorldSafe.Finished(ResearchProjectDef)` is shipped, but there is\nno recipe-level equivalent. So this spec OWES `WorldSafe.RecipeAvailableNow(RecipeDef)`.\"\n\nHalf right. There is no such member in `WorldSafe` — but the recipe-level\nre-derivation ALREADY EXISTS, shipped, as\n`Source/AutoRimmer/MedicalBillVerbs.cs`'s `private static bool RecipeAvailableNow(RecipeDef recipe)`\non `internal static partial class PawnActs` — the same name, clause for clause\nover `WorldSafe.Finished`, including the meme, faction-tag and\n`fromIdeoBuildingPreceptOnly` clauses and the role-apparel unlock. It landed in\n`fc82da6` at 08:11 on 2026-08-31, six minutes after this issue body's last edit,\nwhich is why the recon missed it.\n\nSo 3.6's task is **move it to `WorldSafe` and retarget its one existing caller** —\nnot write it. Writing it fresh forks the catalogue, which is the precise outcome\nthe recon's own \"adding it to WorldSafe (not to a new file) keeps one catalogue\"\nis trying to prevent.\n\n(The underlying hazard is CONFIRMED and worth restating: `RecipeDef.AvailableNow`\n-\u003e `ResearchProjectDef.IsFinished` -\u003e `ProgressReal` -\u003e `ResearchManager.GetProgress`,\nwhich does `progress.Add(proj, 0f)` on a miss into a scribed dictionary. The recon\nalso misses that the SAME method has a second such dictionary —\n`anomalyKnowledge.Add(proj, 0f)` on the Anomaly branch — which the catalogue does\nnot list.)\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 4 — HALF THE STORAGE SURFACE IS ALREADY SCOPED BY 3.2, AND NEITHER\nTHE BODY NOR THE RECON MENTIONS IT\n=====================================================================\n\n`Source/AutoRimmer/ZoneVerbs.cs` (spec 3.2, `57ab92a`, closed and merged) carries\na section literally headed \"WHERE 3.6's BOUNDARY IS\". It already cites\n`RimWorld/ITab_Storage.FillTab` as the priority gate, already ships\n`ParsePriority` and `ApplyPreset`, and already refuses out-of-scope filter edits\nwith a message naming 3.6 (\"storage groups are spec 3.6's (`IStoreSettingsParent`),\nnot this verb's\"). The boundary it draws: presets are a whole-filter REPLACEMENT\nover a fixed five-word vocabulary; anything finer — def-level allow/disallow,\nhit-point and quality ranges, special filters, per-node patches, copy/paste\nbetween storages, storage GROUPS — is 3.6's.\n\nA worker starting from this issue alone will re-implement priority parsing and\ncategory presets from scratch. Put the pointer on the issue.\n\nTwo consequences that follow and are not in either section:\n- `ZoneVerbs.ParsePriority` already excludes `StoragePriority.Unstored`, because\n  `ITab_Storage.FillTab` builds its dropdown with\n  `if (value != StoragePriority.Unstored)`. 3.6's `Building_Storage` path owes the\n  same exclusion, and the spec's \"Priority MUST go through the property\" bullet is\n  silent on the value domain.\n- `RimWorld/ITab_Shells.IsPrioritySettingVisible =\u003e false` (same on\n  `ITab_BiosculpterNutritionStorage`). So setting a PRIORITY on a turret shell\n  holder is a god-hand — the UI does not offer it — and the spec's storage bullet\n  lists \"turret shell filters\" alongside priority. Split them.\n\n=====================================================================\nCONFIRMED — INCLUDING EVERY LINE NUMBER I SAMPLED\n=====================================================================\n\nEvery cited line in the body resolved exactly in this tree: `BillUtility.cs:36`,\n`BillStack.cs:69`, `Bill_Production` fields at 12/14/22/24/26/40, `Bill.cs:29`\n(`suspended`), `Bill_Production.SetStoreMode:197`, `Bill.cs:156`\n(`ingredientFilter.CopyAllowancesFrom(recipe.defaultIngredientFilter)`),\n`StorageSettings.cs:23`, `Building_Storage.cs:100`, `StorageGroupUtility.cs:163`,\n`StorageSettingsClipboard` 16/23/29, `Verse/RecipeDef.cs:241` and `:398`,\n`BillStack.cs:15` (`MaxCount = 15`), `BillStack.cs:87` (`Reorder`). That is an\nunusually good hit rate and worth saying. (Line numbers still do not travel to\nBORGES — the members are `BillUtility.MakeNewBill`, `BillStack.AddBill`,\n`Bill_Production.SetStoreMode`, `Bill.ExposeData`, `StorageSettings.Priority`,\n`Building_Storage.GetStoreSettings`, `BillStack.Reorder`.)\n\n- `BillStack.AddBill` in full: `bill.billStack = this; bills.Add(bill);` —\n  validates nothing. CONFIRMED.\n- The storage-group shadow: `Building_Storage.GetStoreSettings()` is\n  `if (storageGroup != null) { return storageGroup.GetStoreSettings(); } return settings;`\n  with BOTH `settings` and `storageGroup` public fields. CONFIRMED, trap is real.\n- `BillStack.Reorder` guards only `if (num \u003e= 0)`, so moving the last bill down\n  computes `num = Count` and `Insert(Count, ...)` throws after the `Remove`; and a\n  bill not in the stack (`IndexOf` = -1) is INSERTED by any `offset \u003e= 1`. Both\n  halves CONFIRMED.\n- The four-item UI gate: recipe in `def.AllRecipes`; `AvailableNow \u0026\u0026\n  AvailableOnNow(SelTable)` (`ITab_Bills.FillTab`, verbatim); `if (Count \u003c 15)` in\n  `BillStack.DoListing`; and the literal `15` hardcoded rather than `MaxCount`.\n  CONFIRMED — and the literal appears TWICE, the second in `ITab_Bills.FillTab`'s\n  paste gate (`else if (SelTable.billStack.Count \u003e= 15)`), which the recon does not\n  name.\n- The mechanitor/skill dialogs are advisory: in `ITab_Bills.FillTab`'s `Add`\n  delegate the `if`/`else if` chain does not return, and\n  `Bill bill2 = recipe.MakeNewBill(precept); SelTable.billStack.AddBill(bill2);`\n  runs regardless. CONFIRMED.\n- `SetStoreMode` assigns `storeGroup`/`storeMode` BEFORE its consistency check,\n  and the check is `Log.ErrorOnce(\"Inconsistent bill StoreMode data set\", 75645354)`.\n  CONFIRMED (`ErrorOnce`, still a red on first occurrence).\n- The write-on-SAVE narrowing in `Bill.ExposeData` — CONFIRMED verbatim, and it\n  is already in DESIGN's decisions log.\n- `Bill_Production.ShouldDoNow`'s three scribed `paused` writes, and\n  `WorldSafe.BillState(Bill, int)` re-deriving without them. CONFIRMED.\n- No `Rand.*` anywhere in the bill or storage neighbourhood (twelve files\n  checked, unpiped). The only RNG hazard nearby is the inherited `Zone.Cells`\n  shuffle, for which `WorldSafe.ZoneCells` is the shipped route. CONFIRMED.\n- `Zone_Stockpile` does not implement `IStorageGroupMember`, so the group trap is\n  building-only. CONFIRMED.\n- `StorageSettings.Priority`'s setter skips every invalidation when\n  `Current.ProgramState != ProgramState.Playing`. CONFIRMED.\n- Motivation: nothing in 3.1–3.5 creates a production bill; `bills` is read-only;\n  3.4 is medical-only. CONFIRMED by enumerating `[Verb(`.\n- `Alert_NeedMealSource.NeedMealSource` tests only `def.building.isMealSource`.\n  CONFIRMED — plus an UNNAMED extra gate, `if (GenDate.DaysPassed \u003c 2) return false;`\n  in `GetReport`, so it is silent for two days regardless. (Same trap as\n  `Alert_NeedDefenses`; see the 4.1 verification comment, where it is the third\n  known instance.)\n- `Alert_LowFood` has both a 2.5-day floor (`if ((float)Find.TickManager.TicksGame \u003c 150000f)`)\n  and the scarcity threshold `TotalHumanEdibleNutrition \u003c 4f * FreeColonistsSpawnedCount`.\n  CONFIRMED. (Note for anyone reusing that number: the mod's `food_days` divides\n  by colonists PLUS PRISONERS, which mirrors the alert's EXPLANATION text, not its\n  TRIGGER. See the `fc287ba` verification comment — it changes an acceptance\n  there.)\n- The tutorial step: `InstructionDef AddBillSimpleMeal` carries\n  `\u003crecipeDef\u003eCookMealSimple\u003c/recipeDef\u003e`, `\u003crecipeTargetCount\u003e10\u003c/recipeTargetCount\u003e`\n  and the sentence \"Once a bill has been created, colonists will do the work\n  automatically\". Recipe, count and quote all exact. CONFIRMED — but it is the\n  **23rd** `InstructionDef` in the file (18th if you drop the world-gen and\n  character-select entries), not the 11th. Non-load-bearing; do not repeat the\n  ordinal.\n\n=====================================================================\nFIVE THINGS NEITHER SECTION NAMES, TWO OF THEM RED-ERROR PATHS\n=====================================================================\n\n1. **`Bill.SetStoreMode`'s BASE implementation is a red error.**\n   `RimWorld/Bill.cs`:\n   `public virtual void SetStoreMode(...) { Log.ErrorOnce(\"Tried to set store mode of a non-production bill\", 27190980); }`\n   The spec's scope is \"on any `IBillGiver`\", and a `store-mode` verb that takes a\n   bill by index and does not type-test for `Bill_Production` authors a red error\n   the first time it is pointed at a `Bill_Medical` or `Bill_Mech`. The recon\n   caught the MISMATCH error inside `Bill_Production.SetStoreMode` and not this\n   one.\n2. **Editing a storage FILTER emits player-facing messages about BILLS.**\n   `ITab_Storage.FillTab` brackets the filter widget with a before/after\n   `BillUtility.GlobalBills()` diff and fires\n   `\"MessageBillValidationStoreZoneInsufficient\"` for every bill that dropped out.\n   A storage-filter verb that skips it silently drops the game's own warning that\n   a bill's output has nowhere to go — the same \"half a verb\" argument this spec\n   uses to justify bundling storage with bills, turned around. Second-order:\n   `BillUtility.GlobalBills()` can reach\n   `Log.ErrorOnce(\"Found non-bill-giver tagged as PotentialBillGiver\", 13389774)`\n   on a modded bench. (`ColonyVerbs.Bills` correctly avoids that path today by\n   walking the thing group with its own casts.)\n3. **`Bill.CreateNoPawnsWithSkillDialog` stacks a `Dialog_MessageBox`.** The\n   recon's \"report them, do not enforce them\" does not say \"do not CALL it\". A\n   worker reproducing the UI faithfully by calling that helper opens a\n   force-pausing window on a headless bench. The reproducible predicate is\n   `recipe.PawnSatisfiesSkillRequirements(col)` plus `recipe.MinSkillString` for\n   the text; the mechanitor twin is `recipe.mechanitorOnlyRecipe` +\n   `MechanitorUtility.IsMechanitor`. (DESIGN's 2026-08-31 amendment already names\n   this helper from the surgery side and predicts 3.6 inherits it — it does.)\n4. **`ITab_Bills.SelTable =\u003e (Building_WorkTable)base.SelThing;`** — the entire\n   four-item UI gate exists ONLY for `Building_WorkTable`. The spec's scope says\n   \"any `IBillGiver`\", and for a non-worktable bill giver there is no widget gate\n   to reproduce. The spec does not say what to do there. Decide it on-issue.\n5. **`ITab_Storage.IsVisible` carries two gates named nowhere.** The tab is hidden\n   for any selected `Thing` whose `Faction` is non-null and not the player's; and\n   `Building_Grave.StorageTabVisible` is `base.StorageTabVisible ? AssignedPawn == null : false`\n   over `Building_CorpseCasket.StorageTabVisible =\u003e !HasCorpse` — so an occupied or\n   assigned grave has NO storage tab at all. The spec explicitly lists graves.\n\nSmaller: `StorageSettingsClipboard.Copy`/`PasteInto` and the four\n`StorageGroupUtility` link/unlink paths each fire a `Messages.Message` toast, so\n\"gives copy/paste for free\" is true of the LOGIC and not of the player-facing\noutput. And `Building_Storage.AllSlotCellsList()` is\n`return cachedOccupiedCells ?? (cachedOccupiedCells = AllSlotCells().ToList());` —\na cached list rebuilt on read, unscribed and invalidated on spawn/despawn, so\nbenign, but it is the shape the project tracks and `Building_Storage` is new\nsurface for this codebase.\n\n=====================================================================\nACCEPTANCE — REST OF IT\n=====================================================================\n\n- \"add a repeat-forever cook-simple-meal bill, advance, demonstrate meals that did\n  not exist before\" — testable; staging is reachable via `dev:spawn-thing` for a\n  `FueledStove` and raw food (3.3 is still open, so that is the only route). Note\n  `world-fixture bench` will NOT serve — it hardcodes `ThingDefOf.TableButcher`.\n- \"Reorder past the end returns `bad-args` rather than throwing\" — testable, and\n  correctly targeted at a real defect.\n- \"Setting a priority on a grouped `Building_Storage` is visible through the\n  group\" — testable in principle, but **the fixture does not exist and nothing\n  says who builds it.** Greps for `StorageGroup`, `StorageGroupUtility` and\n  `Building_Storage` over `Source/AutoRimmer/` find zero non-comment hits. 3.6\n  must ship the group-link verb AS PART OF its own acceptance fixture; say so,\n  because the group mutator currently appears only as a parenthetical trap note\n  while all the named deliverables are in the Bills section.\n- \"Zero red errors\" — testable, and the concrete surface to dodge is now four\n  items: `Bill.SetStoreMode` base (miss 1), `Bill_Production.SetStoreMode`\n  mismatch, `BillUtility.GlobalBills` (miss 2), and `BillStack.ExposeData`'s two\n  load-time `Log.Error` calls.\n\nOne more from the body that should be sharpened: \"the mutually-exclusive quartet\nat `Bill.cs:165,173,181,189`\" is CONFIRMED as four members\n(`SetPawnRestriction`, `SetAnySlaveRestriction`, `SetAnyPawnRestriction`,\n`SetAnyMechRestriction`) — but there is a **FIFTH**, `SetAnyNonMechRestriction`,\nbacked by the private `nonMechsOnly` field. A verb built to a \"quartet\" spec\ncannot express \"non-mechs only\".\n\n=====================================================================\nWHAT I AM INFERRING, NOT CONFIRMING\n=====================================================================\n\n- That moving `RecipeAvailableNow` to `WorldSafe` is the right shape rather than\n  duplicating it. That is a judgement, though the recon's own stated principle\n  (\"one catalogue\") points the same way.\n- That `Bill.ExposeData`'s narrowing \"converges after one save\". Only `allow: false`\n  is ever written, so it follows — but it is my reading of the loop, not a\n  quoted claim.","files":null}]}